scope: |
  `a-gate-that-starts-a-server-cannot-prove-it-is-talking-to-its-own` is `confirmed: no` — the
  mechanism is real, the instance hypothetical. It asks for identity, and for a PLANT as the proof:
  a foreign listener on the gate's port + the gate's own launcher broken must read RED.

  Ownership, not a nonce and not an allocated port, and the reason is measured: the port is written
  in the EXAMPLE (`examples/health-defaults.ssc` ends in `serve(8769)`), so both of the entry's
  suggestions edit `examples/` to fix a harness problem. Asking the OS which process holds the
  socket needs nothing from the served program. Compared as a process TREE rather than a pid,
  because `bin/ssc` is a launcher script and whether the JVM is the same pid or a child differs by
  lane — a pid comparison would be testing `exec` versus `&`.

  WIDENED to `serve-view-frontend-v2-smoke.sh` before wiring it: that is the gate where the check is
  DECISIVE rather than defence-in-depth. It asserts `http=200` plus a `frontend=` string scraped from
  its own LOG, so a foreign server returning any 200 makes it pass. The gates with body assertions
  (`route-params`, `health-defaults`) would catch a foreign server by its wrong answer; this one
  cannot. Wiring it is what turns the entry's `confirmed: no` into a demonstrated instance.
next: wire serve-view (the DECISIVE one), then health-defaults / std-ui-forms / request-validation

parked: |
  2026-08-14 — the helper, the both-directions self-test and one wired gate are LANDED
  (`route-params-v2-smoke`). Parked at the owner's request to take `install-redundant-build` first;
  the claim is held because the remaining four gates are the same edit and the same verification
  loop, and handing them to somebody else mid-shape would cost more than it saves.

  Landed: `tests/e2e/lib/own-server.sh`, the ownership plant in `no-leaked-servers.sh --self-test`
  (already run by ci.yml), `route-params-v2-smoke.sh`.
  Remaining: `serve-view-frontend-v2-smoke.sh` FIRST — it is the only one where the check is
  decisive rather than defence-in-depth, because it asserts `http=200` plus a string scraped from
  its own log — then `health-defaults-smoke.sh`, `std-ui-forms-smoke.sh`,
  `request-validation-family-gate.sh`.

  Two things measured on the way that the next session should not re-derive:
  - these gates reach for `$ROOT/../bin/ssc-tools`, which a worktree does NOT have (only `bin/ssc`
    is tracked), and none of the five uses `ssc_usable_or_skip` — so instead of a SKIP naming
    `./install.sh --dev` they report "--v1 baseline broke", blaming the product. 20 other gates in
    the directory already source that helper.
  - `route-params-v2-smoke` FLAPS under load: a 30 s deadline while the v2 lane compiles. Same
    failure `health-defaults-smoke` documented when it raised its own 60 → 180.
